# Cursor movement: CUP, HVP, CUU, CUD, CUF, CUB, CNL, CPL, CHA, VPA, HPA, HPR, VPR and the C0
# controls that move the cursor.

test CUP with no parameters goes home
spec xterm ctlseqs: CSI Ps ; Ps H (default 1;1)
size 10 4
feed abc\e[3;5H\e[H
cursor 1,1
screen
|abc       |

test CUP moves to row;column
spec xterm ctlseqs: CSI Ps ; Ps H
size 10 4
feed \e[3;5Hx
cursor 3,6
screen
|          |
|          |
|    x     |

test CUP clamps to the screen
convention every terminal stops at the last row and column; the DEC manuals and ECMA-48 do not say
size 10 4
feed \e[99;99H
cursor 4,10

test CUP treats 0 as 1
spec ECMA-48 8.3.21: a parameter of 0 selects the default
size 10 4
feed \e[3;5H\e[0;0H
cursor 1,1

test CUP with only a row keeps column 1
spec xterm ctlseqs: omitted parameters default to 1
size 10 4
feed \e[3;5H\e[2H
cursor 2,1

test CUP with only a column keeps row 1
spec xterm ctlseqs: omitted parameters default to 1
size 10 4
feed \e[3;5H\e[;7H
cursor 1,7

test HVP is CUP
spec xterm ctlseqs: CSI Ps ; Ps f
size 10 4
feed \e[2;4fx
cursor 2,5
screen
|          |
|   x      |

