test CUU stops at the top margin when the cursor is inside the region
spec VT510 CUU: the cursor stops at the top margin
known-fail: alacritty – CUU and CUD ignore the scrolling margins and run to the edge of the screen
size 10 5
feed \e[2;4r\e[4;1H\e[9A
cursor 2,1

test CUD stops at the bottom margin when the cursor is inside the region
spec VT510 CUD: the cursor stops at the bottom margin
known-fail: alacritty – CUU and CUD ignore the scrolling margins and run to the edge of the screen
size 10 5
feed \e[2;4r\e[2;1H\e[9B
cursor 4,1

test CUU above the region goes on to the first row
spec VT510 CUU: above the top margin the cursor stops at the top line
size 10 5
feed \e[3;4r\e[2;1H\e[9A
cursor 1,1

test CUD above the region still stops at the bottom margin
spec VT510 CUD: the cursor stops at the bottom margin
known-fail: alacritty – CUU and CUD ignore the scrolling margins and run to the edge of the screen
size 10 5
feed \e[2;3r\e[1;1H\e[9B
cursor 3,1

test CUD below the region goes on to the last row
spec VT510 CUD: below the bottom margin the cursor stops at the bottom line
size 10 5
feed \e[2;3r\e[4;1H\e[9B
cursor 5,1

test backspace moves left one column
spec VT510 control table BS: moves the cursor one position to the left; ECMA-48 8.3.5
size 10 4
feed ab\b
cursor 1,2
screen
|ab        |

test backspace stops at the first column
spec VT510 control table BS: at the left margin no action occurs
size 10 4
feed \b\b
cursor 1,1

test carriage return goes to the first column
spec ECMA-48 8.3.15 CR
size 10 4
feed abc\r
cursor 1,1

test line feed moves down and keeps the column
spec VT510 LNM: with LNM reset the cursor moves to the current column of the next line
size 10 4
feed ab\ncd
screen
|ab        |
|  cd      |
cursor 2,5

test vertical tab and form feed act as line feed
spec VT510 LNM: LF, FF and VT move the cursor to the next line
size 10 4
feed a\vb\fc
screen
|a         |
| b        |
|  c       |

test new line mode makes line feed also return the carriage
spec VT510 LNM: with LNM set LF, FF and VT move to the first column of the next line
known-fail: alacritty – LF does not return the carriage when LNM (CSI 20 h) is set
size 10 4
feed \e[20hab\ncd
screen
|ab        |
|cd        |
cursor 2,3

test NEL moves to the start of the next line
spec ECMA-48 8.3.86 NEL: ESC E
size 10 4
feed ab\eEcd
screen
|ab        |
|cd        |

test IND moves down and keeps the column
spec VT100 User Guide IND: ESC D
size 10 4
feed ab\eDcd
screen
|ab        |
|  cd      |

test RI moves up and keeps the column
spec ECMA-48 8.3.104 RI: ESC M
size 10 4
feed \e[3;4H\eMx
cursor 2,5
screen
|          |
|   x      |

test control characters inside a sequence still act
spec vt100.net/emu/dec_ansi_parser: C0 controls are executed during a control sequence
size 10 4
feed ab\e[2\n;3Hx
screen
|ab        |
|  x       |
cursor 2,4

test NUL and DEL are ignored
spec vt100.net/emu/dec_ansi_parser: NUL is executed (no effect), DEL (7F) is ignored; ECMA-48 8.3.88 NUL
size 10 4
feed a\x00b\x7fc
screen
|abc       |
cursor 1,4

test bell prints nothing and does not move the cursor
spec ECMA-48 8.3.3 BEL
size 10 4
feed a\ab
screen
|ab        |
cursor 1,3

test IND at the bottom margin does not scroll a cursor outside the left and right margins
spec VT510 IND with DECLRMM: the region scrolls only for a cursor inside its columns; esctest2 IND_MovesDoesNotScrollOutsideLeftRight
known-fail: alacritty – the region scrolls although the cursor is outside the left and right margins
size 10 6
feed \e[2;5r\e[?69h\e[2;5s\e[5;3Hx\e[5;6H\eD
cell 5,3 text=x
cursor 5,6
feed \e[5;1H\eD
cursor 5,1
cell 5,3 text=x

test RI at the top margin does not scroll a cursor outside the left and right margins
spec VT510 RI with DECLRMM: the region scrolls only for a cursor inside its columns
known-fail: alacritty – the region scrolls although the cursor is outside the left and right margins
size 10 6
feed \e[2;5r\e[?69h\e[2;5s\e[2;3Hx\e[2;6H\eM
cell 2,3 text=x
cursor 2,6

test CBT goes past the left margin
spec esctest2 CBT_IgnoresRegion: the tab stops before the cursor are all the stops there are, margins or not
size 40 4
feed \e[?69h\e[5;30s\e[1;7H\e[2Z
cursor 1,1

test BS and CUB go back to the line above with reverse wraparound (45) only if it wrapped
spec xterm ctlseqs: CSI ? 45 h, reverse-wraparound mode (needs DECAWM); only to a line that wrapped into this one
known-fail: alacritty – no reverse wraparound (modes 45 and 1045)
size 10 4
feed abcdefghijkl\e[?45h\b\b\b
cursor 1,10
feed \e[2;1H\b
cursor 1,10
feed \r\n\e[3;1H\b
cursor 3,1

test reverse wraparound (1045) goes back over a line that did not wrap and round the top
spec xterm ctlseqs: CSI ? 1045 h, extended reverse-wraparound mode
known-fail: alacritty – no reverse wraparound (modes 45 and 1045)
size 10 4
feed \e[?1045h\e[3;1H\b
cursor 2,10
feed \e[1;1H\b
cursor 4,10
feed \e[2;3r\e[2;1H\b
cursor 3,10

test reverse wraparound goes to the right margin
spec xterm ctlseqs: CSI ? 1045 h with left and right margins
known-fail: alacritty – no reverse wraparound (modes 45 and 1045)
size 20 4
feed \e[?1045h\e[?69h\e[5;10s\e[3;5H\b
cursor 2,10
feed \e[3;1H\b
cursor 2,10

test reverse wraparound needs autowrap
spec xterm ctlseqs: reverse-wraparound mode only works in conjunction with DECAWM
size 10 4
feed \e[?7l\e[?45h\e[?1045h\e[3;1H\b
cursor 3,1

test a backspace in the delayed wrap with reverse wraparound only ends the wait
convention the cursor waiting to wrap is one column beyond the last, so BS lands on the last column (esctest2 ReverseWrapStartingInDoWrapPosition)
known-fail: alacritty – no reverse wraparound (modes 45 and 1045)
size 10 4
feed \e[?45habcdefghij\bX
screen
|abcdefghiX|
feed \e[?45l\e[2;1Habcdefghij\bX
screen
|abcdefghiX|
|abcdefghXj|

test CUB with reverse wraparound walks back like backspace
spec xterm ctlseqs: reverse-wraparound applies to CUB (esctest2 DECSET_ReverseWraparound_Multi)
known-fail: alacritty – no reverse wraparound (modes 45 and 1045)
size 10 4
feed \e[1;9Habcd\e[?45h\e[4D
cursor 1,9
